  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1235 PM CDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nThe subtropical ridge that offered just enough wiggle room for \ntoday's front to move through will be restrengthening over Texas \nnext week. Aside from the minimal chance for a small seabreeze \nshower over the Coastal Plains, that should squelch rain chances for \nthe week. Southerly winds will return and dew points will steadily\nclimb, resulting in more hot and humid air. Highs will stay in \nthe 90s to low 100s with peak heat indices around 98 to 106 for \nmost areas each day. Continue to practice heat safety and stay \ncool and hydrated.",
